            <ArticleTitle>Patient education in pain control.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>148-55</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Patients' concerns about reporting pain and using analgesics have been cited as major contributors to the problem of inadequate pain management. The purpose of this paper is to describe a program of research in which we have focused on these patient concerns, or as we refer to them, &quot;patient-related barriers to pain management.&quot; We present a summary of descriptive studies on this topic, describe educational interventions that have been tested, and suggest future avenues of research and practice.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
